## What I Would Validate First — And Why

**Experiment 0: Run a Single Custom Static-Musl ARMv6 Executable in Native Android Shell.**

Before building loop images, chroots, or installing packages, compile a simple "Hello World" or a statically linked `busybox` / `dropbear` binary using an ARMv6 static toolchain (`arm-linux-musleabi`), push it to `/data/local/tmp/`, and execute it directly via the existing root shell.

**Why:**
This single test takes 5 minutes and immediately proves whether custom binaries can run on kernel 2.6.35 without floating point exceptions, kernel syscall panics, or ABI mismatches. It bypasses all mount, filesystem, and chroot complexities and instantly confirms your compiler toolchain settings for all future work.
